-- title:
--   Graded pieces of an ideal of products are bounded by the recursive splitting sum
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $G$ an additive abelian group, $w:\sigma\to G$ a weight function and $R=K[x_\sigma]$. For $d\in G$ let $R_d$ be the space of polynomials that are weighted homogeneous of weight $d$ (every monomial $x^m$ occurring has $\sum_sm_sw(s)=d$), and assume that **every** $R_d$ is finite-dimensional. For an ideal $J$ put $Q_d(J)=R_d/(J\cap R_d)$, and call $J$ *component-closed* if it contains the weight-$d$ component of each of its elements, for every $d$.
--
--   A *factor pair* $q$ consists of polynomials $\ell_q,r_q\in R$ and weights $\delta_q,\delta'_q\in G$ such that $\ell_q$ is weighted homogeneous of weight $\delta_q$ and $r_q$ is weighted homogeneous of weight $\delta'_q$. For a finite list $\mathbf q=(q_1,\dots,q_M)$ of factor pairs let $P(\mathbf q)$ be the ideal generated by the products $\ell_{q_1}r_{q_1},\dots,\ell_{q_M}r_{q_M}$, and define the *splitting bound* $S(I,d,\mathbf q)\in\mathbb{N}$ recursively by $S(I,d,\varnothing)=\dim_KQ_d(I)$ and
--   $$S(I,d,(q,q_2,\dots,q_M))=S\bigl(I+(\ell_q),\,d,\,(q_2,\dots,q_M)\bigr)+S\bigl(I+(r_q),\,d-\delta_q,\,(q_2,\dots,q_M)\bigr).$$
--   Then for every component-closed ideal $I$, every list $\mathbf q$ and every $d\in G$,
--   $$\dim_K Q_d\bigl(I+P(\mathbf q)\bigr)\ \le\ S(I,d,\mathbf q).$$
--
--   Unwinding the recursion, $S(I,d,\mathbf q)$ is a sum of $2^M$ terms, one for each way of choosing either $\ell_{q_k}$ or $r_{q_k}$ from every pair; each term is the dimension of a graded piece of the ideal generated by $I$ and the chosen factors, in the degree $d$ shifted by the weights $\delta_{q_k}$ of the pairs whose right factor was chosen. The theorem thus reduces the Hilbert function of an ideal of products of homogeneous polynomials to ideals generated by single factors, and is the starting point of a multihomogeneous Bézout-type count.
--
--   **Formalization Note** A factor pair is the structure `FactorPair w` (fields `left`, `right`, `leftDegree`, `rightDegree` and the two homogeneity proofs). $P(\mathbf q)$ is `productIdeal w qs`, defined recursively by adding one principal ideal per pair; $S$ is `splitBound w I d qs`; $Q_d$ is `componentQuotient` and dimensions are `Module.finrank K`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Algebra/Determinantal/Multigraded.lean#L181-L212

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SmoothInitialForm
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Algebra_Determinantal_Multigraded

open OAI OAI.PermanentBorder OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded
open MvPolynomial
variable {K σ G : Type*} [Field K] [AddCommGroup G]
variable (w : σ → G)

theorem OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded.finrank_le_splitBound [∀ d, Module.Finite K (Piece (K := K) w d)]
    (qs : List (FactorPair (K := K) w)) (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial σ K))
    (hI : ComponentClosed w I) (d : G) :
    Module.finrank K (componentQuotient w (I ⊔ productIdeal w qs) d) ≤
      splitBound w I d qs := by sorry
